<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greco-Persian Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Greek Wars, Persian Wars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greco-Persian Wars were a series of conflicts in the fifth century BCE between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-city-states">Greek city-states</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>. Persian invasions of mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> were repulsed at battles such as Marathon, Salamis and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a>. For the Achaemenid Empire the wars marked the western limit of its expansion and shaped later Greek views of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars.jpg" alt="Greco-Persian Wars" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greek-Persian_duel_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section><h2 class="enc-section-title">Mentioned in 2 profiles</h2><div class="enc-mentions"><a href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire<span class="secs">Military, Decline</span></a><a href="/empire/miletus">Miletus<span class="secs">Summary</span></a></div></section>
